Use `useChatRuntime` from `@assistant-ui/ai-sdk` and pass the runtime to `<AssistantRuntimeProvider>`, with `<Thread />` inside. This is for `ai@^7` and `@ai-sdk/react@^4`. There are separate legacy pages for v4–v6, which I didn't read.

Your route should read `messages` (`UIMessage[]`) from the request, pass `await convertToModelMessages(messages)` to `streamText`, and return:

```ts
return createUIMessageStreamResponse({
  stream: toUIMessageStream({ stream: result.stream }),
});
```

The default transport is `AssistantChatTransport`. For an endpoint other than the default, use `new AssistantChatTransport({ api: "/my-custom-api/chat" })` as `transport`. It also sends `system` and frontend `tools`. To use them, pass `system` to `streamText` and wrap `tools` in `frontendTools()`. If you have tools, also pass them to `convertToModelMessages`. For multiple tool-call steps, set `stopWhen`, for example `stepCountIs(10)`.

Pages: docs/runtimes/ai-sdk/v7.md
